<newsitem itemid="531473" id="root" date="1997-04-23" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Samgro lifts yr shr, div.</title>
<headline>Samgro lifts yr shr, div.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>		 (millions of rand unless indicated)</p>
<p>Shr (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline	    17.88  vs   15.39</p>
<p>    - attrib		32.66  vs   29.27</p>
<p>    Final div (cts)     7.41  making 13.70 vs 12.53</p>
<p>    Total income	  67.68  vs   52.08</p>
<p>    Interest earned     28.25  vs   18.08</p>
<p>    Dividends received  13.90  vs   12.58</p>
<p>Other operating</p>
<p>    income		  25.53  vs   21.43</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		 66.19  vs   51.42</p>
<p>    Tax			9.78  vs    6.25</p>
<p>Div payable July 2</p>
<p>on register May 23</p>
<p>Full name: Samgro Investment Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE: The group said that the planned merger of NBS and Boland Bank as well as the strategic alliance with the Board of Executors created exciting possibilities. It derives most of its income from its 64.93 percent stake in Boland Bank.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
